# Guardrails policy (process-options.md "Tier-conditional guardrails") — which
# sessions get the vendored guardrails core prepended, keyed by model substring.
# One value on the last line:
#   off               — never (the current setting).
#   all               — every session.
#   all except <sub>  — every session except the named frontier model(s).
#   <sub> [<sub> ...] — an allowlist (e.g. `sonnet` to guard just the quick tier).
#
# SET TO `off` (WI-107): guarding requires the vendored docs/guardrails/core.md
# (from the guardrails sibling repo TheColliny/FableClaudeMDForOpus, drift-checked
# by check_vendored.py). That content is owner-ruled to live upstream and pulled
# downstream via the vendoring layer — NOT built in this kit repo (docs/status.md
# "External follow-up"), so no core.md is present here. A guarding token (e.g.
# `sonnet`) with no core would draw agent_loop's "running without the guardrails
# core" warning every run; `off` is the honest state until the core is vendored.
# Flip to `sonnet` (guard the quick tier) once docs/guardrails/core.md lands and
# check_vendored.py is green.
off
